{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 64, :comments ["<b>But among these there was not any man of them whom Moshe and Aharon the priest numbered</b> — for Yehoshua and Kalev were not included in this census, because they were sixty years old and above, and the counting is only from twenty years old up to sixty years old, for those are the prime years of a man, as stated in the valuations (Leviticus 27:3), and at that age he goes out to the army in Israel, but not from sixty and above, according to the words of our Sages (Bava Batra 121a). But Scripture says, <b>and there remained not a man of them, save Kalev the son of Yefunneh and Yehoshua the son of Nun</b> — because they were among those counted in the first census and did not die."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Ramban first explains why Yehoshua and Kalev are excluded from the phrase 'of them whom Moshe and Aharon the priest numbered' (the second census), and then notes that the subsequent verse nevertheless lists them as survivors, because they belonged to the first census."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:10.194705272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}